1.Why Testing Matters?
  ->Testing is the process of verifying that software works correctly and meets business requirements. In Salesforce, Apex testing helps ensure that new features do not introduce bugs into existing functionality.
 Benefits of Testing
* Improves software reliability
* Prevents production issues
* Validates business logic
* Reduces maintenance costs
* Ensures application stability
* Supports safe deployment
Enterprise systems rely heavily on testing because even small errors can affect thousands of users.
2. What is Asynchronous Processing?
  -->Asynchronous processing allows tasks to run in the background without making users wait for completion.
  ->Instead of executing everything immediately, the system processes long-running tasks separately.
Examples of Asynchronous Apex
* Future Methods
* Queueable Apex
* Batch Apex
* Scheduled Apex
Benefits
* Faster user experience
* Better scalability
* Handles large workloads
* Prevents system timeouts
* Improves performance
Important Test Cases for College Management System
1. Invalid Email Format
a. Test
  ->Enter an incorrectly formatted email address.
b. Prevents
  ->Invalid student contact information being stored.
 2. Duplicate Student Registration
a. Test
  ->Attempt to register the same student twice.
b. Prevents
  ->Duplicate records and inaccurate reporting.
 3. Course Seats Exceed Limit
a. Test
  ->Register students beyond available seats.
b.Prevents
  ->Overbooking of courses.
 4. Missing Required Fields
a.Test
  ->Submit registration without mandatory information.
b. Prevents
  ->Incomplete records.
 5. Attendance Below Threshold
a. Test
  ->Student attendance falls below minimum requirement.
b.Prevents
  ->Incorrect eligibility calculations.
 6. Faculty Assignment Validation
a. Test
  ->Assign a course without a faculty member.
b. Prevents
  ->Unmanaged courses.
 7. Formula Field Accuracy
a. Test
  ->Verify attendance percentage calculations.
b.Prevents
  ->Incorrect reporting and decisions.
 8. Notification Delivery Failure
a. Test
  ->Simulate notification processing issues.
b.Prevents
  ->Missed alerts and communication failures.

4. Async Use Cases?
 1. Bulk Email Sending
  ->Sending thousands of confirmation emails should happen in the background.
Benefit
  ->Users do not wait for email delivery.
2. Report Generation
  ->Generating large reports can take significant time.
 Benefit
  ->Improves user experience.
 3. Large Data Import
  ->Processing thousands of records should be asynchronous.
Benefit
  ->Prevents timeouts.
 4. Notification Processing
  ->Alerts and notifications can be queued.
 Benefit
  ->Improves system responsiveness.
 5. External System Synchronization
  ->Integrating with external applications often requires background processing.
 Benefit
  ->Reduces delays and improves reliability.
